Package: omx-panel
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: nodejs (>= 18), omx-contract-data (>= 3.20.2~), plugin-hostd-contract (>= 0.20.7~), omx-dsp-wasm (>= 0.33.0~), omx-contract (>= 3.20.2~), omx-panel-contract (>= ${source:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: plugin-hostd (>= 0.20.7~)
# omx-modgui-sync lists the LV2 plugins with lilv; Debian bookworm has no python3-lilv (trixie and later do), so it is a suggestion
Suggests: python3-lilv
Description: panels for LV2 and CLAP plugins, generated from what each plugin declares
 omx-panel makes panels for LV2 and CLAP plugins from what each plugin
 declares. It lays a panel out from a plugin's descriptor (sections, controls,
 roles, the pages of eight a controller shows), writes a MOD GUI for MOD and
 Zynthian in the omx look, imports a plugin's own MOD GUI into a skin package,
 and carries the skin package schema, its validator and the directory skin
 packages are installed into. The omx-panel command runs each; the tools are
 under /usr/share/omx-panel for a build that calls them.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

Package: libomx-panel-render0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, omx-panel (= ${source:Version})
Description: omx-panel renderer, a library that draws a panel into a pixel buffer
 libomx-panel-render.so.0 draws a panel description in the omx look into a CPU
 pixel buffer and answers input with the one gesture vocabulary. A surface
 loads it at run time (Zynthian's panel view); its look, geometry and fonts
 are omx-panel's.

Package: libomx-panel-render-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libomx-panel-render0 (= ${binary:Version}), libcjson-dev, ${misc:Depends}
Description: omx-panel renderer, development files
 The headers omx_panel_render.h and omx_panel_gesture.h, the
 libomx-panel-render.so link and the omx-panel-render pkg-config file, to
 build against the omx-panel renderer and its gesture reference.

Package: libomx-panel-store0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, omx-panel-contract (>= ${source:Version})
Description: descriptions store of panel descriptions, the library
 libomx-panel-store.so.0 reads and writes the descriptions store: the base,
 the system layer and the user layer of panel.sqlite, merged in that order of
 precedence, its words checked against the panel domain.

Package: libomx-panel-store-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libomx-panel-store0 (= ${binary:Version}), libsqlite3-dev (>= 3.38.0~), libcjson-dev, libomx-domain-dev (>= 3.20.0~), ${misc:Depends}
Description: descriptions store of panel descriptions, development files
 The header omx-panel/omx_panel_store.h, the libomx-panel-store.so link, the
 omx-panel-store pkg-config file and the store's DDL (panel.sql), to build
 against the descriptions store.

Package: omx-panel-store
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, omx-panel-contract (>= ${source:Version})
Description: descriptions store of panel descriptions, the command
 The command omx-panel-store gets, puts and removes an entry of the
 descriptions store (the base, the system layer and the user layer of
 panel.sqlite) and checks the layers; omx-panel's tools and the console's
 server call it.

Package: omx-panel-contract
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: panel domain: the words a panel description speaks
 The panel domain (contract.d/panel): the families, widgets, display kinds,
 display sources and placements a panel description speaks, with their
 translations, installed into the contract directory where omx-contract's
 loader reads it, and its codes header omxdomain/panel_codes.h. A program that
 reads the panel words depends on this package.

